= How a quantity is put together =

A quantity in OSW is assembled from four kinds of pages. Knowing which is which tells you how much work a given change actually is.

{| class="wikitable"
!Page
!Namespace
!Type
!Holds
|-
|'''Unit'''
|Item
|[[:Category:OSW6c2aea028a8647cd97f5d7c65c09cd44|Composed Unit]]
|One unit, for example [[Item:OSWf101d25e944856e3bd4b4c9863db7de2|Metre]]. Its conversion factor to the SI unit, its symbol, and a list of scaled variants (millimetre, kilometre, ...) as subobjects under <code>composed_units</code>.
|-
|'''Quantity kind'''
|Item
|[[:Category:OSW00fbd6feecb5408997ca18d4e681a131|Quantity Kind]]
|What is being measured, for example length. Lists the units that may express it.
|-
|'''Characteristic'''
|Category
|[[:Category:OSWc7f9aec4f71f4346b6031f96d7e46bd7|Fundamental Quantity Value Type]]
|The building block you actually put into a category, for example [[:Category:OSWee9c7e5c343e542cb5a8b4648315902f|Length]]. Carries the default unit, the units offered in the editor, and the semantic property the value is stored under.
|-
